Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 10:07:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Custom animated tab icons + Service Detail scrolling parallax
 hero
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bottom navigation — replaced generic icons with custom SVG icons that
morph when a tab activates, per request:
- Home: a door that swings open on its hinge
- Services: a 2x2 grid whose blocks expand outward from center
- Jobs: a briefcase whose lid flips open
- Inbox: a chat bubble whose message dots pop in
- Profile: a face whose eyes open from closed to a full circle
All built with react-native-svg + reanimated (useAnimatedProps),
wrapped in the existing AnimatedTabIcon for the scale-bounce + sliding
active-pill background from the previous pass.

Service Detail screen — fixed the sticky hero image bug and gave it a
proper professional treatment:
- Root cause: the hero image lived in a View OUTSIDE the ScrollView,
  so it never moved while the body scrolled beneath it. Moved it
  inside the ScrollView as the first item so it scrolls away
  naturally with the rest of the content.
- Added a subtle parallax + zoom-on-pull-down effect on the hero via
  useAnimatedScrollHandler/useAnimatedStyle.
- Added a floating header bar (back + bookmark, always accessible)
  that's transparent over the image and fades to a solid surface
  color with the service title once scrolled past the hero — matches
  the polished collapsing-header pattern used by Airbnb/Uber-style
  detail screens.

Full typecheck (skillbuddy + libs): zero errors.

Still outstanding from the live-testing round: an exhaustive header
styling pass across every remaining screen, and verification of
directional back/forward navigation animations app-wide.
